Wait, the block calculation changed. Originally it was `(N + threads * 4 - 1) / (threads * 4)` because each thread processes 4 elements. With vectorized loads, each thread processes VEC_SIZE elements (8 for half). The number of vectorized work items is `num_vecs`, and with 256 threads per block, we need `(num_vecs + 255) / 256` blocks.

